 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? It varies a lot by weather and how fast you' going. In cold weather, perspiration can lead to being dehydrated. So drinking before you start is important. Fill a water bottle with wet ice before you leave, and top it up midway. A light band on your handlebars is also helpful so you can see it as you take sips. Definitely. A bar or sandwich left too long can get cold. A small bag of crackers and cheese is great too. You can, and many people do. But a full stomach makes you a lot more tired, so it's worth having a small something just after waking.",
